-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. WEIGHTS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
In KNN , all attributes of an object equally contribute to calculate 
the distance between this vector to other vectors. However, in reality, 
some attributes might be less important than others in order to determine
the difference (distance) betwen two object. So in some cases, the less 
important attributes can influence on the distance rather the important ones.

The problem can be limited by weighting the contribution of each attribute. So
that the some attributes will have more impact the result and some will have 
less than. 

Question:

- If all the values of a dimension are the same, 
  how good is that dimension as a clasifier?

- Discuss what weights give the best classification?

Hint :

Define a vector weight 

 create function weights()->vector of number;
 set weights() = {1,1,1,1,1,1,1,1,1};

Then distance function should take weights into account

 distance(x*weights(), disfn, dispara, v),


